vements to confirm they do not violate any clearance rules.\n\n\nAnalysis focuses on three specific camera shots within the defined environment. Each shot description includes frame ranges, beats, track section identifiers, and car velocity data. The go\n<truncated 2532 bytes>\nion, and camera position, capturing the whip-orbit transition and high-to-low dive into the corkscrew section.\n\n\nAnalyzing `Cam_S16_BottomOutPullout`, focusing on the high-speed compression and transition, considering the spark effects at the rear quarter. This will track the velocity change as it transitions from a steep angle to zero degrees, incorporating the portal glitch. `Cam_S17_TunnelPortalEntry` will examine the hyper-speed chase within the strobe tunnel. The analysis centers on FOV warp and speed, specifically at the tunnel entry.\n\n\nAnalyzing `Cam_S17_TunnelPortalEntry`, the focus is on the hyper-speed chase and FOV warp at the tunnel entry. This is followed by assessment of `Cam_S18_TunnelCockpitStrobe`, focusing on the cockpit view inside the cyber-tunnel. Finally, `Cam_S19_TunnelWhipOrbit180` demands examining the `180°` whip-orbit inside the tunnel as it exits at high speed.\n\n\nFocusing on the harbor brake impact sequence, the analysis proceeds through two distinct camera shots. The initial shot captures the car's blinding exit, heavy braking, and impact, specifically highlighting the blazing carbon brake discs. The second shot then focuses on an ultra-close macro of the front wheel and rotor at the hairpin apex.\n\n\nAnalysis of the final shots begins with `Cam_S22_HarborLaunchChase`, focusing on the launch from the hairpin exit, tracking the wet-rooster-tail effect and upshift exhaust star-cones. Shot `Cam_S23_SkylineSideSweep` involves low-angle diagonal tracking, emphasizing the Nueva York 2099 skyline. The final shot, `Cam_S24_FinishGantryRise`, captures the dramatic pull-up, tilt-up, and fade-out as the car crosses the finish line.\n\n\nThe requested shots from `#3