{"step_index":284,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T08:25:27Z","input_tokens":6728,"cache_read_tokens":474464,"output_tokens":34820,"thinking":"The manifest export, initiated directly from the composition script, appears to be functioning correctly, creating a clean coordination path. This allows for direct transfer of 3D camera data to the effects pipeline. The initial test seems successful in linking composition and effects.\n\n\nThe direct dependency on the track data allows for immediate generation of the shots manifest. This eliminates the need to wait for environment processing, enabling `@sfx` to access 3D camera positions without delay. Now, the focus shifts to writing the updated composition, still, and render scripts, starting with detailed verification of the composition script's input specifications and functionality.\n\n\nThe track data's JSON file is being read to extract cyclic points and timing information for generating a $C^2$-smooth track representation. The script ensures smoothness at the wrap point by appending the same point with a full lap time. The shared 3D banked ribbon basis definition is being checked, specifically the cross product between the tangent and ribbon vectors; initial testing identified a sign discrepancy, requiring a verification of the `@track` calculations.\n\n\nThe orthonormal basis, derived from the track data, is confirmed as right-handed with a determinant of +1.  The calculations, including the cross product and dot product verifications, confirm the basis's properties. This right-handed nature is consistent with the car rig's orientation.\n\n\nThe car's local secondary motion components are being stepped at a constant 12 fps, distinct from the 24 fps linear motion of the bone heading rotation and camera focus. Intense visual effects, like titanium spark streaks, are specifically triggered during high-speed, uphill G-compression and heavy kerb riding, with particular focus on specific compression zones. Lighting receivers for the car objects, along with the camera focus, are being updated at 24 fps.\n\n\nThe `track_pt_clamped` function computes the target lateral position relative to the centerline, clamping the camera's position within specified limits based on tunnel sections and other constraints. This function guarantees the camera's position remains within `±6.4 m` of the track's centerline, effectively framing shots even on banked sections. This provides a robust solution for diverse camera setups, including chase, orbit, and fixed shots, automatically adjusting for track banking and hill pitch.\n\n\nThe camera's positional constraints are designed to prevent collisions with environmental barriers and architectural elements, ensuring shots remain within defined boundaries. The camera's banked road normal ensures that horizon and banking tilt produce cinematic visuals without flipping, utilizing different blending approaches. A built-in self-check verifies camera occlusion and cinema-scope framing.\n\nThe `Comp_V6_SpiderVerse` compositor leverages ray tracing for realistic reflections on the asphalt, enhancing the visual fidelity of the scene. The exposure fade curve is specifically adjusted to maintain clarity throughout the specified frame range.\n\n\nThe exposure issue in the specified frame range stems from an outdated keyframe in an earlier build, now corrected by setting explicit keyframes at the beginning, end, and fade-out frames. This ensures consistent exposure across the entire timeline. Further refinements include high-contrast color curves, halftone screen effects, painterly sky treatments, chromatic aberrations, and speed lines.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nV6 SPIDER-VERSE 3D MEGA-CIRCUIT ANIMATION, 24 BLOCKBUSTER CAMERAS & 2.39:1 COMPOSITOR\\n=====================================================================================\\n赛道数据: track_data/spiderverse_circuit.json\\n          (Neo-Monaco x Nueva York 2099 Sky-Harbor / 3.72 km / ΔZ=+42.35 m / 17.4° Bank /\\n           53.3333 s / 96 Beats @ 108 BPM / 1,281 Frames @ 24 fps)\\n输入工程: v6_spiderverse/v6_stage_lookdev.blend   (只读输入，100% 隔离 V5)\\n输出工程: v6_spiderverse/v6_stage_anim_sv.blend\\n相机清单: v6_spiderverse/v6_shots_manifest.json\\n\\n用法:\\n  python pipeline/v6_sv_comp.py --manifest-only\\n  blender -b -P pipeline/v6_sv_comp.py\\n  blender -b -P pipeline/v6_sv_comp.py -- --test 35,282,413,414,635,960,1041,1067,1068,1134\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport json\\nimport math\\nimport os\\nimport sys\\nfrom math import sin, cos, pi, radians, degrees, sqrt, exp, atan2\\n\\nPROJ = r\\\"D:\\\\项目session\\\\blender-supercar\\\"\\nTRACK_JSON = os.path.join(PROJ, \\\"track_data\\\", \\\"spiderverse_circuit.json\\\")\\nMANIFEST_OUT = os.path.join(PROJ, \\\"v6_spiderverse\\\", \\\"v6_shots_manifest.json\\\")\\n\\nARGV = sys.argv[sys.argv.index(\\\"--\\\") + 1:] if \\\"--\\\" in sys.argv else sys.argv[1:]\\n\\n\\ndef argval(flag, default=None):\\n    if flag in ARGV:\\n        i = ARGV.index(flag)\\n        if i + 1 < len(ARGV) and not ARGV[i + 1].startswith(\\\"--\\\"):\\n            return ARGV[i + 1]\\n        return True\\n    return default\\n\\n\\nMANIFEST_ONLY = bool(argval(\\\"--manifest-only\\\", False))\\nIN_BLEND = argval(\\\"--in\\\", os.path.join(PROJ, \\\"v6_spiderverse\\\", \\\"v6_stage_lookdev.blend\\\"))\\nOUT_BLEND = argval(\\\"--out\\\", os.path.join(PROJ, \\\"v6_spiderverse\\\", \\\"v6_stage_anim_sv.blend\\\"))\\nTEST_FRAMES = argval(\\\"--test\\\", None)\\n\\nos.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(OUT_BLEND)), exist_ok=True)\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# 0. 读取三维高程+倾角赛道数据并构建精确 C2 闭环插值器\\n# ---------------------------------------------------\n<truncated 77828 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"d:\\\\项目session\\\\blender-supercar\\\\pipeline\\\\v6_sv_comp.py\""}}],"truncated_fields":["to